WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.488 --> 00:00:02.729
- Most people look at law school

00:00:02.729 --> 00:00:05.083
as some inscrutable ivory tower.

00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:07.861
As a result, there are
a huge number of myths

00:00:07.861 --> 00:00:10.191
about what happens when
you start law school.

00:00:10.191 --> 00:00:13.651
So today let's talk about some
of the three biggest myths

00:00:13.651 --> 00:00:17.651
about starting law school
and why they're wrong.

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:22.984
So let's dive into the biggest myths

00:00:22.984 --> 00:00:25.059
about starting law school.

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:28.392
The first myth is, "Everybody
knows what they want to do

00:00:28.392 --> 00:00:29.734
"when they graduate."

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.102
In reality, very few
people go to law school

00:00:32.102 --> 00:00:35.307
knowing exactly what they
want to do when they graduate

00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:36.489
from law school.

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:38.036
You may have a general idea that you want

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:39.627
to go into public interest law,

00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:41.844
or you want to become a civil litigator,

00:00:41.844 --> 00:00:44.096
or you want to go into criminal defense.

00:00:44.096 --> 00:00:47.551
But very few people know
exactly the sub field,

00:00:47.551 --> 00:00:50.290
exactly the firm that they want to go to.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.412
In fact, most people will
change their conception

00:00:53.412 --> 00:00:56.046
of what they want to
do when they graduate.

00:00:56.046 --> 00:00:58.536
So don't be afraid to go to law school

00:00:58.536 --> 00:01:01.681
not knowing exactly which firm

00:01:01.681 --> 00:01:04.611
and which section of
law you want to practice

00:01:04.611 --> 00:01:05.997
when you graduate.

00:01:05.997 --> 00:01:08.309
In reality, very few
people know exactly what

00:01:08.309 --> 00:01:12.371
they want to do and those
things change over time.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.830
Now on the other hand, you
should have a general idea

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.514
and you should be damn sure
that you definitely want

00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:20.489
to be a lawyer or you
want to go into some field

00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:23.566
that requires a law degree
before you go to law school.

00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:27.783
It's a huge waste to go to law
school not knowing for sure

00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:30.570
that you in fact want to do something

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.297
that requires a law degree.

00:01:32.297 --> 00:01:35.689
Law school these days cost
hundreds of thousands of dollars.

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:37.678
It can cost over $200,000

00:01:37.678 --> 00:01:39.828
when you factor in living expenses.

00:01:39.828 --> 00:01:43.845
So that is a huge penalty to
pay if you aren't 100% sure

00:01:43.845 --> 00:01:47.077
that you want to be a lawyer
or you need a law degree

00:01:47.077 --> 00:01:49.118
for the field that you want to go into.

00:01:49.118 --> 00:01:51.886
So while you don't need to know
exactly what you want to do,

00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:55.251
it's a good idea to know
that you do absolutely

00:01:55.251 --> 00:01:56.376
need a law degree.

00:01:56.376 --> 00:01:58.091
Law school is not the time to figure out

00:01:58.091 --> 00:01:59.883
what you want to do with your life.

00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:02.203
So that takes me to myth number two.

00:02:02.203 --> 00:02:05.521
And that is, "Everyone
is super competitive."

00:02:05.521 --> 00:02:07.739
Now certainly there are going to be a lot

00:02:07.739 --> 00:02:09.526
of competitive people.

00:02:09.526 --> 00:02:12.776
But not everyone is a cutthroat gunner.

00:02:14.285 --> 00:02:18.067
Just like in undergrad, there
is a huge spectrum of people

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.161
who on one side are
incredibly competitive,

00:02:21.161 --> 00:02:23.438
and on the other side
are complete slackers.

00:02:23.438 --> 00:02:25.675
And while there certainly
aren't as many slackers

00:02:25.675 --> 00:02:28.411
in law school as there are in undergrad,

00:02:28.411 --> 00:02:30.757
they certainly get into law school.

00:02:30.757 --> 00:02:33.708
A corollary to the myth that
everyone is super competitive

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:37.337
is the myth that everyone
is incredibly mean.

00:02:37.337 --> 00:02:40.434
On the contrary, I find
that law students in general

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:41.912
are a very kind bunch.

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:44.717
And some of my best friends
are the people that I met

00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:45.790
in law school.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.211
So don't think that you're
going to go into law school

00:02:48.211 --> 00:02:50.132
and everyone is going to
have their nose buried

00:02:50.132 --> 00:02:53.611
in a book all day long focused on nothing

00:02:53.611 --> 00:02:55.816
but acing their exams.

00:02:55.816 --> 00:02:58.111
Certainly by the time
that finals come around

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.561
everyone is probably going
to cocoon themselves,

00:03:00.561 --> 00:03:02.645
but for the most part
law students are people

00:03:02.645 --> 00:03:05.058
just like everybody else.

00:03:05.058 --> 00:03:07.481
And not everyone is going to be

00:03:07.481 --> 00:03:11.783
a super A plus type personality
that doesn't care anything

00:03:11.783 --> 00:03:13.276
about anyone else.

00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:16.311
Then number three is that,
"Everyone has legal experience

00:03:16.311 --> 00:03:17.850
"before they go to law school."

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:21.505
Or in other words, "Everybody
knows this stuff but me."

00:03:21.505 --> 00:03:22.533
Not true.

00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:25.288
In fact, very few people
have legal experience

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:26.944
before they go to law school.

00:03:26.944 --> 00:03:29.460
There are a handful of people
who work as paralegals,

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.182
or legal secretaries,
but here's the secret.

00:03:33.182 --> 00:03:36.443
Even if you had those jobs
before you went to law school,

00:03:36.443 --> 00:03:39.514
that does not prepare you for
the law school experience.

00:03:39.514 --> 00:03:41.808
And it doesn't make you
a very good law student.

00:03:41.808 --> 00:03:44.110
On the contrary, the
kind of day-to-day things

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:47.520
that paralegals do and
legal secretaries do,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.279
the only thing I think
it would be helpful for

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:51.119
is civil procedure.

00:03:51.119 --> 00:03:53.791
Other than that, they probably
have no further insights

00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:56.039
into the substantive law
that's gonna be tested

00:03:56.039 --> 00:03:58.206
as a 1L than anybody else.

00:03:59.056 --> 00:04:03.578
So, in fact, very few people
have legal experience.

00:04:03.578 --> 00:04:06.595
And even the people that
do have legal experience,

00:04:06.595 --> 00:04:08.789
it's not the kind of experience
that's going to help them

00:04:08.789 --> 00:04:10.072
as a law student.

00:04:10.072 --> 00:04:12.489
So don't worry about gunners.

00:04:13.725 --> 00:04:15.840
Gunners are very vocal.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.303
They seem like they know
what they're talking about,

00:04:17.303 --> 00:04:20.357
but for the most part
they're actually less likely

00:04:20.357 --> 00:04:22.464
to do well than everybody else.

00:04:22.464 --> 00:04:25.286
So if you did not have legal
experience before going

00:04:25.286 --> 00:04:27.598
to law school, don't worry about it.

00:04:27.598 --> 00:04:29.784
It's not going to help the
people that do have it.

00:04:29.784 --> 00:04:33.013
And it's not a hindrance
to you not having it.

00:04:33.013 --> 00:04:34.721
If you like this video, please click like

